<title>USA: USDATA Corp chief executive resigns.</title>
<headline>USDATA Corp chief executive resigns.</headline>
<dateline>RICHARDSON, Texas 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDATA Corp on Monday said William Moore Jr resigned as president and chief executive officer in order to return to his consulting practice.</p>
<p>He would remain a consultant to the company through 1997, USDATA said.</p>
<p>Moore would be succeeded by Bill Newell as acting CEO, the company said.</p>
<p>Newell is now a vice president of Safeguard Scientifics Inc, the company said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
